> A calculation before fitting

Predictions0,4 and targets2,6 give squared errors4,4. With fitting-scale SD2, normalized mean squared error is(4+4)/(2*4)=1.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lstm_forecast_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;double computed=n::mean(n::square((n::tensor({0.,4.})-n::tensor({2.,6.}))/2.)).item(),analytic=1.;if(std::abs(computed-analytic)>2e-6)throw std::runtime_error("hand calculation differs from native primitives");std::print("| native calculation | analytic reference |\n|---:|---:|\n| {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",computed,analytic);dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(std::vector<double>{0,1},std::vector<double>{computed,analytic},"worked reference",{37,99,235}).ylim(0,std::max(.5,std::max(computed,analytic)*1.2)).x_label("0 = native calculation;1 = analytic reference").y_label("Toy objective or diagnostic value").title("lstm forecast hand calculation").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/lstm_forecast_worked.svg");}
