> Actual rolling-origin forecasts

The three direct horizons use only the12 past observations. Target years and values come from the held-out archive; curves use observation units, rather than normalized training loss. This is a reconstructed chronological split.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lstm_forecast_predictions.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto load=[](const std::string&path){auto a=dm::nn::load_npz(path);return std::map<std::string,dm::nn::Tensor>(a.begin(),a.end());};auto out=load("build/nn-completion/models/lstm_forecast/outputs.npz"),data=load("build/nn-completion/models/lstm_forecast/data.npz");auto pred=out.at("prediction").to_vector<double>(),truth=data.at("test_target").to_vector<double>(),origins=data.at("test_origins").to_vector<double>();auto layout=dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,3);for(int h=0;h<3;++h){std::vector<double>x,y,z;for(size_t i=0;i<origins.size();++i){x.push_back(origins[i]+h);y.push_back(truth[i*3+h]);z.push_back(pred[i*3+h]);}auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.lines(x,y,"observed",{37,99,235}).lines(x,z,"direct forecast",{234,88,12}).x_label("Target year").y_label("Original yearly sunspot units").title("Horizon "+std::to_string(h+1));layout.add(plot);}layout.size(1500,500).fit_panels().save_svg("build/lstm_forecast_predictions.svg");}
